<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">canonical projection</h1>

<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<br class="ltx_break">
<p class="ltx_p">Given a group <math id="p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline"><mi>G</mi></math> and a <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">normal subgroup</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/NormalSubgroup.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/normalsubgroup"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup> <math id="p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\lhd G" display="inline"><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⊲</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></math> there is an <a class="nnexus_concepts" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="this.nextSibling.style.display='inline'">epimorphism</a><sup style="display: none;"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Epimorphism.html"><img src="http://mathworld.wolfram.com/favicon_mathworld.png" alt="Mathworld"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/epi"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/abeliancategory"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/typesofhomomorphisms"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/typesofmorphisms"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/grouphomomorphism"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/ringhomomorphism"><img src="http://planetmath.org/sites/default/files/fab-favicon.ico" alt="Planetmath"></img></a></sup></p>
<table id="S0.SS0.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S0.SS0.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\colon\thinspace G\to G/N" display="block"><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="4.2pt">:</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="ltx_p">defined by sending an element <math id="p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></math> to its coset <math id="p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="gN" display="inline"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁢</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></math>. The epimorphism <math id="p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline"><mi>π</mi></math> is referred to as the <em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><a class="nnexus_concept" href="http://planetmath.org/canonicalprojection">canonical projection</a></em>.
</p>
